Keje is an API-only Laravel app and ships no Blade templates, but this
directory must still exist.

Laravel resolves views from resource_path('views') by default, and
`php artisan view:cache` — run by the Deploy API workflow and included in
`php artisan optimize` — fails outright when the directory is missing:

    The ".../apps/api/resources/views" directory does not exist.

Git does not track empty directories, so this placeholder is what keeps it
present after a `git reset --hard` on the deploy host. Delete it only if you
also stop running view:cache/optimize.
